  <html:p>A <fr:link href="/ZUVW/" title="Mixture of Experts (MoE)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/ZUVW/" display-uri="ZUVW" type="local">Mixture of Experts (MoE)</fr:link> has <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[E]]></fr:tex> experts and top-<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[k]]></fr:tex> routing, int8 weights on a TPU v5e (ridge point around 240 FLOPs/byte). What batch size does it need to be compute-bound, and what is that for DeepSeek v3?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:strong><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B > 120E/k]]></fr:tex> tokens.</html:strong> For DeepSeek v3, with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[E = 256]]></fr:tex> routed experts and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[k = 8]]></fr:tex>, that is <html:strong><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B > 3840]]></fr:tex> tokens</html:strong> — a startlingly large batch to require at generation time.

  <html:strong>Per weight matrix:</html:strong> a full batch touches every expert, so all <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[E]]></fr:tex> copies get loaded — <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[EDF]]></fr:tex> bytes — while only <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[k]]></fr:tex> experts fire per token, so the work is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[2kBDF]]></fr:tex> FLOPs. The <fr:link href="/YBQD/" title="Arithmetic intensity" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/YBQD/" display-uri="YBQD" type="local">arithmetic intensity</fr:link> is therefore

  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\frac {2kBDF}{EDF} = \frac {2kB}{E}]]></fr:tex>

  and int8 weights against bf16 arithmetic need that above roughly 240, giving <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[kB/E > 120]]></fr:tex>.

  <html:strong>The framing that makes this obvious:</html:strong> an MoE is a dense model with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[E]]></fr:tex> MLP blocks per layer. Total parameters scale with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[E]]></fr:tex>; parameters activated per token scale with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[k]]></fr:tex>. The sparsity <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[E/k]]></fr:tex> — typically 8 to 64, and 32 for DeepSeek v3 — is exactly the factor by which the required batch inflates. The other cost is routing: two <fr:link href="/T470/" title="AllToAll" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/T470/" display-uri="T470" type="local">AllToAlls</fr:link> per MoE block, out to the experts and back.
</html:details>
